Tell whether a camera reached through PipeWire failed after its capture started, and why

PipeWire's capture module (the Camera portal's path on Linux) returns from StartCapture as
soon as its stream is asked to connect; the camera is linked to it afterwards, by the
session manager. A camera that cannot stream then, for example a V4L2 camera another
application streams (its VIDIOC_S_FMT answers EBUSY), fails the link: WirePlumber 0.5
sends the stream that link's error ("error set output format: -16 (Device or resource
busy)", in the sound server's language), which reached only WebRTC's log, and the
application showed a black picture. The module now keeps the first error its stream was
told since StartCapture and its last state, and VideoCaptureModule::CaptureFailed (on the
API thread, as CaptureStarted) tells them: whether the capture failed, with the error, or
else what the stream is doing. The other modules tell a failure as StartCapture returns
and answer false. The wrapper waits for a camera's start with it
(patches/wrapper/0028).

diff --git a/modules/video_capture/linux/video_capture_pipewire.cc b/modules/video_capture/linux/video_capture_pipewire.cc
index 2f4eb55..bf2a4db 100644
--- a/modules/video_capture/linux/video_capture_pipewire.cc
+++ b/modules/video_capture/linux/video_capture_pipewire.cc
@@ -232,6 +232,14 @@ int32_t VideoCaptureModulePipeWire::StartCapture(
 
   pw_stream_add_listener(stream_, &stream_listener_, &stream_events, this);
 
+  {
+    // What an earlier stream said is not this one's.
+    MutexLock lock(&api_lock_);
+    failed_ = false;
+    error_.clear();
+    state_ = "unconnected";
+  }
+
   spa_pod_builder builder =
       spa_pod_builder{.data = buffer, .size = sizeof(buffer)};
   std::vector<const spa_pod*> params;
@@ -289,6 +297,14 @@ bool VideoCaptureModulePipeWire::CaptureStarted() {
   return started_;
 }
 
+bool VideoCaptureModulePipeWire::CaptureFailed(std::string& why) {
+  RTC_DCHECK_RUN_ON(&api_checker_);
+  MutexLock lock(&api_lock_);
+
+  why = failed_ ? error_ : std::string("PipeWire stream ") + state_;
+  return failed_;
+}
+
 int32_t VideoCaptureModulePipeWire::CaptureSettings(
     VideoCaptureCapability& settings) {
   RTC_DCHECK_RUN_ON(&api_checker_);
@@ -410,12 +426,21 @@ void VideoCaptureModulePipeWire::OnStreamStateChanged(
   RTC_DCHECK(that);
 
   MutexLock lock(&that->api_lock_);
+  that->state_ = pw_stream_state_as_string(state);
   switch (state) {
     case PW_STREAM_STATE_STREAMING:
       that->started_ = true;
       break;
     case PW_STREAM_STATE_ERROR:
       RTC_LOG(LS_ERROR) << "PipeWire stream state error: " << error_message;
+      // Kept for CaptureFailed: the first error says why the camera did not
+      // stream (WirePlumber 0.5 sends the stream a link that failed, such as
+      // "error set output format: -16 (Device or resource busy)" for a V4L2
+      // camera another application streams). Later ones follow from it.
+      if (!that->failed_) {
+        that->failed_ = true;
+        that->error_ = error_message ? error_message : "PipeWire stream error";
+      }
       [[fallthrough]];
     case PW_STREAM_STATE_PAUSED:
     case PW_STREAM_STATE_UNCONNECTED:
